# redisx AI Rules

## Coding Style

- Always prefer functional programming patterns using `samber/lo` and `samber/mo` where applicable.
- Avoid using global locks (`sync.Mutex` / `sync.RWMutex`) on critical hot paths; prefer connection-scoped context or atomic operations.
- Avoid using global variables unless explicitly asked.
- Always try to use a function instead of creating a new struct

## Test

- Always use `testify/suite` to organize and manage test lifecycles.
- Eat own dog food: avoid mocking internal components whenever possible; test against real instances (e.g., real BuntDB, real Server/Client).
- Strongly prefer Table-Driven Tests (TDT) to cover logical branches and edge cases comprehensively.
- feature driven(json)
